1
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:07,700
Forty-seven tabs. Twelve job boards. One resume… and zero replies.

2
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:33,367
And that's a problem most college students face. Internships get posted late. Networking events are buried on LinkedIn. Your inbox fills up with jobs that have nothing to do with you. Nothing helps you honestly tailor your resume to each new opening. Tracking it all during a busy semester is a job of its own. And reaching professionals in your field? That's the hardest part.

3
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:48,633
For TCU students, the search is scattered — across Handshake, LinkedIn, and dozens of company sites. Tailoring every application takes hours. And there are only so many advising slots.

4
00:00:49,567 --> 00:00:51,233
Don't hunt for a job alone.

5
00:00:52,900 --> 00:01:01,800
We're TCU students. We lived this. So we set out to turn every student's background into real decisions — and real next steps.

6
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:14,633
Meet Remy. A personal AI career coach that finds the roles that fit you — and helps you go after them, honestly.

7
00:01:15,567 --> 00:01:17,833
Start with what you already have.

8
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:23,300
Remy asks what you want — not the other way around.

9
00:01:28,700 --> 00:01:33,233
Then it finds real, open roles — and your strongest match for each.

10
00:01:36,367 --> 00:01:49,633
Step three. Remy tailors your resume for each job you apply to. First, it asks you a few questions. Then it rewrites your real experience, in your words, to match what that posting asks for.

11
00:01:51,033 --> 00:02:05,833
Here's exactly what changed. On the left, what the posting requires. On the right, your resume, before and after. Every edit maps to a requirement. And if a detail is missing, Remy flags it and asks you, instead of making it up.

12
00:02:07,700 --> 00:02:13,800
One resume for everything doesn't work. So every position gets its own version, tuned to that role.

13
00:02:16,700 --> 00:02:25,600
Then it writes a custom cover letter for each one. Not a template with the company name swapped in, but your own story, tied to what that company is looking for.

14
00:02:30,033 --> 00:02:33,000
You see your score — and exactly why it moved.

15
00:02:35,367 --> 00:02:40,133
It connects you with TCU alumni in your field, and helps you write the first email.

16
00:02:43,700 --> 00:02:46,633
Every application and deadline, in one place.

17
00:02:48,700 --> 00:02:58,767
And Remy keeps getting better. Every draft is checked against your real resume. Every review makes those checks sharper. So each version is stronger than the last.

18
00:03:00,367 --> 00:03:01,800
And it's live today.

19
00:03:10,367 --> 00:03:11,867
And this is just the start.

20
00:03:15,700 --> 00:03:21,800
Every student should understand their options — and build a path that's theirs. Don't hunt for a job alone.

